            <ArticleTitle>[Conditioned reactions and mediator-humoral shifts during neurotization in a probabilistic pain reinforcement situation].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1197-1206</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Substitution of regular partial reinforcement for random one (in both cases the reinforcement frequency was 50%) acted in some dogs as a neurotizing factor: they showed unrest, stable defensive reflexes disappeared, corresponding changes were observed in vegetative reactions. At the same time activation of the sympatho-adrenal system was recorded along with a drop in concentration of acetylcholine in peripheric blood. It is noted that the development of neurotic disturbances in dogs in these conditions were to a certain degree dependent of the dominating motivation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
